    "name": "Witch Doctor: flat/percent self passives with no stat scaling work natively (#803, #1011, #1067, #2893)",
    "contract": "Four unrelated single-target-less Witch Doctor self passives, none touched by any AscensionWitchDoctor* module code, spell_script_names row or SCRIPT_EFFECT (all four ids grepped clean across modules/mod-ascension-compat, src/server/scripts and data/sql in this session). Presence of the Loa 572871 (#803): one SPELL_AURA_MOD_CRIT_PCT (290) effect, MiscValue 0, BasePoints 3 (real 4, DieSides 1). Player::UpdateSpellCritChance (StatSystem.cpp:967-986) sums SPELL_AURA_MOD_CRIT_PCT unconditionally into every school's PLAYER_SPELL_CRIT_PERCENTAGE field, and AuraEffect::HandleAuraModCritPct (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:4892) triggers Player::UpdateAllWeaponDependentCritAuras, whose Player::UpdateWeaponDependentCritAuras (Player.cpp:7325) sets a flat mod added unconditionally (via the aura-type check in its lambda) into PLAYER_CRIT_PERCENTAGE for base/off/ranged attacks; both paths are pure sums, so the crit fields move by exactly the aura's Amount with no other floating-point interaction. Dark Mojo 712396 (#1011): two SPELL_AURA_MOD_DEBUFF_RESISTANCE (178) effects, MiscValue 2 (DISPEL_CURSE) and 1 (DISPEL_MAGIC), both BasePoints 19 (real 20). Consumed in Unit::MagicSpellHitResult (Unit.cpp:3719-3720) via GetMaxPositiveAuraModifierByMiscValue/GetMaxNegativeAuraModifierByMiscValue keyed on the incoming spell's own Dispel field, re-read in this session; no harness metric exposes that resist-chance contribution directly (only a statistical miss-rate sample over many casts would observe it, per apps/coa-gameplay-test/README.md's metric catalog), so this scenario asserts the deterministic part instead: the self-aura applies/removes correctly and each effect's own live percentage (aura_amount) matches the DBC-derived tooltip number. Spiritual Traditions 705911 (#1067): SPELL_AURA_REDUCE_PUSHBACK (149, MiscValue 4, BasePoints 69, real 70) and SPELL_AURA_MOD_MANA_REGEN_INTERRUPT (134, BasePoints 39, real 40) are both tooltip-documented and asserted; a third effect (SPELL_AURA_DUMMY, MiscValue 19, real amount -5) is untooltipped, has no script binding and is intentionally left unasserted (recorded in .agents/plans/audit-witchdoctor/observations.md). Spell::Delayed (Spell.cpp:7958-7963) computes delayReduce = 100 + GetTotalAuraModifier(SPELL_AURA_REDUCE_PUSHBACK) - 100, i.e. exactly the aura's own Amount, then AddPct(delaytime=500, -delayReduce): with Amount=70 this is int32(500 * -70.0f/100.0f) = -350, so delaytime becomes exactly 150 (CalculatePct/AddPct in Util.h are simple float truncations, verified in this session), matching the scenario's exact assertion. The mana-regen clause (Player::UpdateManaRegen, StatSystem.cpp:1090-1094) writes UNIT_FIELD_POWER_REGEN_INTERRUPTED_FLAT_MODIFIER, a field no harness metric reads, so only its aura_amount is asserted (its live application/removal is still proven by the aura presence check). Alchemical Enhancement 705921 (#2893): SPELL_AURA_HASTE_SPELLS (216, BasePoints 4, real 5) and SPELL_AURA_MOD_MELEE_RANGED_HASTE (192, MiscValue 127, BasePoints 4, real 5). AuraEffect::HandleModCastingSpeed (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:4915) calls Unit::ApplyCastTimePercentMod, which divides UNIT_MOD_CAST_SPEED by (100+Amount)/100; SpellInfo::CalcCastTime multiplies a SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_MAGIC spell's cast time by that same field (SpellInfo.cpp:2948, Unit::ModSpellCastTime), so a magic-class probe spell's spell_cast_time_ms must fall. AuraEffect::HandleModMeleeRangedSpeedPct (SpellAuraEffects.cpp:4939) calls Unit::ApplyAttackTimePercentMod unconditionally for all three WeaponAttackTypes, which writes UNIT_FIELD_BASEATTACKTIME + hand directly, exactly what the attack_time_ms metric reads. Malefic Wrath 807037 is used as the magic-class cast-time probe (SpellFamilyName 19/WD, SpellFamilyFlags[0]=0 so the WD-specific Agility cast-time branch in Unit::ModSpellCastTime does not apply to it, DmgClass SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_MAGIC, base cast time 2000ms per SpellCastTimes.dbc id 5) instead of a Witch Doctor's own damage spells, all of which turned out to carry DmgClass SPELL_DAMAGE_CLASS_RANGED and would be driven by ranged attack speed, not spell haste; Fire Blast 2136 (learnable by any class, used the same way by existing primalist scenarios) is the instant hostile probe used to trigger Spell::Delayed for the pushback clause, mirroring apps/coa-gameplay-test/scenarios/primalist-whispers-cave-dweller.json's proven pattern and its map-0 test coordinates. All DBC fields for all four spells and the probe spells were re-verified directly against the installed Spell.dbc/SpellCastTimes.dbc via coa-dbc-viewer in this session.",
